<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανα-βαίνω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαμβ-</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Opp.
			<u>H.</u>
			3.638
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>get up on,
				mount,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					1487
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				169
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαναβεβηκότες</span>
			<i>mounted</i> (on horseback), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.85
			</span></i>; of a star, <i>rise above the horizon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				342b34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of animals,
				<i>cover,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				540a22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Clearch.
				36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>come upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ γῆρας ἐπαναβάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					612
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>go up</i> inland, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>to be promoted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὰς τῶν ταξιάρχων χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					2.1.23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτίαι</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχαί,</span>
			<i>mount upwards,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὰ ἀνωτέρω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					990a6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				257a22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἐπαναβεβηκός</span>
			<i>higher</i> or <i>more ultimate principle,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.174
			</span></i>; the <i>genus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.6
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχῆς] οὐδεὶς ἂν εὕροι ἁπλουστέραν
					οὐδὲ ἐπαναβεβηκυῖαν ἡντινοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					2.9.1
				</span></i>
			; <i>search for higher principles,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ἀεὶ εἰς ἄπειρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.6.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαναβεβηκότα τῇ ψυχῇ
			[νοῦν</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.9.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>transcend,</i> c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>in Prm.</u>
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.Mus.</u>
				47.617
			</span></i>; also c. dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέργεια -βεβηκυῖα
				πάσαις καὶ χρωμένη αὐταῖς ὡς ὀργάνοις</span>
		ibid.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
